:[{"end":77,"id":"1379921727422046208","start":65,"username":"clockworkio"},{"end":147,"id":"3116631887","start":135,"username":"ITPressTour"}],"urls":[{"description":"At the IT Press Tour, Clockwork explains why large GPU clusters fail, how FleetIQ detects faults, and how AI training can recover without lost work.","display_url":"techtalksnetwork.com/blog/why-ai-cl…","end":272,"expanded_url":"https://techtalksnetwork.com/blog/why-ai-clusters-fail-clockwork","images":[{"height":941,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2109748235619168256/LTNESQNf?format=png&name=orig","width":1672},{"height":150,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2109748235619168256/LTNESQNf?format=png&name=150x150","width":150}],"start":249,"status":200,"title":"Why Clockwork Wants AI Clusters to Fail Without Stopping | The Tech Talks Network | Enterprise Tech Podcasts","unwound_url":"https://techtalksnetwork.com/blog/why-ai-clusters-fail-clockwork","url":"https://t.co/TJMsvFpXP8"},{"display_url":"pic.x.com/IUb1iwPaXt","end":303,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/NeilCHughes/status/2109764798736916990/video/1","media_key":"13_2109733537410605056","start":280,"url":"https://t.co/IUb1iwPaXt"}]},"id":"2109764798736916990","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":11,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"How reliable is a 1,024-GPU training job? Meta research cited by @clockworkio shows a mean time to failure of 7.9 hours. \n\nRecorded on @ITPressTour, the team explained why detection, restarts, and recomputation turn failures into an AI ROI problem. https://t.co/TJMsvFpXP8  #ITPT https://t.co/IUb1iwPaXt","url":"https://x.com/NeilCHughes/status/2109764798736916990"},{"author_id":"774645390666764288","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:49:43.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109763469285183817"],"id":"2109763469285183817","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":8,"like_count":1,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"AI Hardware Explained (Part 5)\n(This is a short version.)\n\nNVL72 === A rack named NVL, and it has 72 GPUs.\n\nHOW DO THEY TALK TO EACH OTHER?\n\nWe discussed this earlier.\nNVL72 means that the rack contains 72 GPU packages, wired together to act like a big giant chip. And that rack","url":"https://x.com/agentNirmites/status/2109763469285183817"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["13_2109763694985187328"]},"author_id":"3378986176","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:54:11.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109764594701066639"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/JqARXI037b","end":303,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/andrew_n_carr/status/2109764594701066639/video/1","media_key":"13_2109763694985187328","start":280,"url":"https://t.co/JqARXI037b"}]},"id":"2109764594701066639","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":1,"impression_count":211,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":2,"retweet_count":0},"text":"One small change to the actor update makes RL work for flow policies on real robots, VLAs, and even image models. Here's QF3 from UC Berkeley and Amazon FAR, explained in 4 minutes!!!\n\nA lot of robots today run on flow policies. A flow policy turns random noise into an action by https://t.co/JqARXI037b","url":"https://x.com/andrew_n_carr/status/2109764594701066639"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2109762606307123200"]},"author_id":"111724748","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:46:40.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109762703245877354"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/hiGKZPfOmo","end":299,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/Deadmeatz/status/2109762703245877354/photo/1","media_key":"3_2109762606307123200","start":276,"url":"https://t.co/hiGKZPfOmo"}]},"id":"2109762703245877354","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":9,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"TODAY'S AI NEWS IS ABSOLUTELY INSANE\n\nHere's a full recap — October 12th, 2026  \n\n1. Meta Unveils Muse Wonder — Its Most Powerful AI Models Yet, Challenging OpenAI a